# The build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, not this directory — paths below are
# written from there. Without these lines a local .venv and the whole .git
# history are uploaded to the daemon on every build: slow, and a way for secrets
# to reach an image layer.
#
# Named after the Dockerfile beside it: BuildKit reads
# <dockerfile-name>.dockerignore from the Dockerfile's own directory, and it
# takes precedence over a .dockerignore at the context root.

.git
.github
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
dist
build
*.egg-info

# Secrets and local state.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*credentials*.json
*token*.json

# Nothing here runs in the image. `docker/` included: the Dockerfile is read by
# the client through -f, not copied from the context. `devenv/` even more so —
# it is by definition the half that never leaves this machine.
docker
devenv
docs
examples
notebooks
tests
db
evals
scripts
*.md
!README.md
